---
// smaqmd-aer-find-ratings — "Where to find an air cleaner's ratings", the disclosure
// that tells someone where the CADR / air-flow number actually lives on a product.
// Titled as a statement, not a question: it leads the cleaners step (before the
// fields exist to ask about) and must read the same on the result step's mount.
//
// It is ONE component mounted TWICE (the cleaners step, where the number is being
// asked for, and the result step, where a shopper is about to go looking for one)
// precisely so the two copies cannot drift: the same words, in both places the
// question comes up. Its vanilla twin is the pair of <details> blocks in
// public/aer-tool/index.html — KEEP IN SYNC with those when the copy changes.
//
// Because it mounts twice, NOTHING in here may carry an `id`: two copies of the
// same id is a duplicate-id defect even when only one is on screen. The disclosure
// is esa-collapsible (native <details>/<summary>), so it needs none.
import EsaCollapsible from '@esa/ecology/esa-collapsible.astro';
// The label photo lives in public/ (shared with the vanilla twin), so Astro will
// NOT rewrite its path for the production `base` — withBase() does it.
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';
---

<EsaCollapsible title="Where to find an air cleaner's ratings">
  <div class="stack" data-gap="sm">
    <p class="typography-body-md smaqmd-aer-find__lede">
      Look for the CADR (Clean Air Delivery Rate) or air flow rating, in CFM (ft³/min):
    </p>
    <!-- Own list class, NOT the wizard's .smaqmd-aerb__tips: that rule is scoped to
         smaqmd-aer-wizard.astro and would not reach a separate component's markup
         anyway — reaching for it would only look like reuse. -->
    <ul class="typography-body-md smaqmd-aer-find__list">
      <li>
        On the front of the box — the AHAM Verifide label lists three CADR
        numbers (tobacco smoke, dust, pollen). Use the lowest, usually Tobacco
        Smoke.
      </li>
      <li>On a specifications panel on the side or the back of the box.</li>
      <li>In the manual, in the specifications section.</li>
      <li>
        On the manufacturer's website — search the model number and open its
        specifications page.
      </li>
      <li>
        If it only lists air changes per hour (ACH), also note the room size
        that rating was measured in — the tool asks for both.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <!-- The label photo. `alt` says WHERE ON THE PRODUCT the rating appears and
         which of the three numbers to use — it IS the instruction for anyone who
         cannot see it, so it carries the same guidance the <figcaption> does.
         width/height match the file's intrinsic 1200×645 so the box reserves
         its space and the disclosure does not jump when the image decodes.
         IF THE PHOTO IS EVER SWAPPED: update both, and keep the alt locating +
         instructing.
         bcn-lego-checked: no esa- lego is a captioned image/media block — the
         catalog's image-bearing legos are esa-avatar (a circular person chip) and
         esa-empty-state (an illustration + heading + action for a zero state),
         neither of which is a figure with a caption; checked Beacon (no
         figure/media component in its shared ui-* set). So the figure is native
         HTML with a documented smaqmd- block around it. -->
    <figure class="smaqmd-aer-find__figure">
      <img
        src={withBase('/aer-tool/aham-label.jpg')}
        alt="AHAM Verifide label on the front of an air cleaner box. Under the suggested room size, the section titled Clean Air Delivery Rate Tested lists three circled CADR numbers — Tobacco Smoke 189, Dust 196, Pollen 191. The lowest, 189, is the one to use."
        width="1200"
        height="645"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="typography-body-md">
        The AHAM Verifide label on the front of the box — the three circled CADR
        numbers are what this tool asks for; use the lowest (here, Tobacco
        Smoke).
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- Two more real labels, side by side where the width allows: the layout
         varies box to box, so a shopper sees the pattern (room size on top,
         three CADR numbers below) rather than one box's exact design. Same alt
         discipline as the hero figure: the alt IS the instruction. -->
    <div class="smaqmd-aer-find__examples">
      <figure class="smaqmd-aer-find__figure">
        <img
          src={withBase('/aer-tool/aham-label-100sqft.jpg')}
          alt="A second AHAM Verifide label, on a smaller air cleaner's box: suggested closed room size 100 square feet, then three CADR numbers — Tobacco Smoke 62, Dust 68, Pollen 65. The lowest is Tobacco Smoke, 62."
          width="769"
          height="784"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="typography-body-md">
          A smaller unit's label — same three numbers; the lowest here is
          Tobacco Smoke, 62.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="smaqmd-aer-find__figure">
        <img
          src={withBase('/aer-tool/aham-label-246sqft.jpg')}
          alt="A third AHAM Verifide label: suggested closed room size 246 square feet, then three CADR numbers — Tobacco Smoke 159, Dust 167, Pollen 170. The lowest is Tobacco Smoke, 159. The fine print notes the suggested room size is based on 4.8 air changes per hour."
          width="800"
          height="789"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="typography-body-md">
          Another box — its fine print confirms the printed room size assumes
          4.8 air changes per hour.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</EsaCollapsible>

<style>
  /* Quiet supporting copy — the same rung the wizard's result text sits at, so a
     disclosure opened inside either surface reads as part of it. */
  .smaqmd-aer-find__lede,
  .smaqmd-aer-find__list {
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464);
  }
  .smaqmd-aer-find__list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem);
  }
  .smaqmd-aer-find__list li + li { margin-block-start: var(--spacing-200, 0.5rem); }
  .smaqmd-aer-find__figure { margin: 0; }
  /* The image RESERVES its box before it loads — the width/height attributes
     give the browser each photo's intrinsic ratio (the figures are different
     shapes), so opening the disclosure does not reflow when a photo decodes.
     The token-tinted ground shows while it loads. */
  .smaqmd-aer-find__figure img {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.5rem);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken, #f0f0f0);
  }
  /* The two extra examples share a row when the disclosure is wide enough for
     two ~12rem columns, and stack below that. */
  .smaqmd-aer-find__examples {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(12rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--spacing-300, 0.75rem);
  }
  .smaqmd-aer-find__figure figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--spacing-200, 0.5rem);
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464);
  }
</style>
